// alloc — package-level bump allocator over one qualified `Extent`
// (wiki/spec/resources/allocation.md, TASKS.md BUMP-ALLOCATOR-CANARY).
//
// The package owns only the allocation strategy: `bump.omg` carries the
// qualified-extent partition contract (`ExtentPartition`), the bump policy
// (`Bump`/`Issued`/`Attempt`), the tail-ward `release` and full-return
// `reset`, and the `BumpVec` reservation container with its finite
// `RetiredSlot`. The compiler owns no allocator semantics here: every
// extent the strategy touches is `Extent in Granted & Vacant`, and custody
// is conserved through the boundary's authored `separate`/`embed` laws.
// Establishing residents still waits on the placed-access operations the
// strategy's `Vacant` requirements pin.
//
// The durable depend-edge consumer is
// `tests/omega/pass/memory/bump_allocator_canary`.
use bump;
